<title>UK: GEC /Finmeccanica co-operating, no take-over.</title>
<headline>GEC /Finmeccanica co-operating, no take-over.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's General Electric Co Plc and Finmeccanica SpA, said on Monday that their discussions on co-operation in the defence sector were continuing successfully.</p>
<p>&quot;However, following recent reports in the UK press, both companies wish to make clear that this co-operation does not involve either company acquiring the other's defence interests,&quot; the two companies said in a statement from GEC.</p>
<p>GEC was caught up in fierce speculation ahead of a long-awaited review on Tuesday when managing director George Simpson publishes his plan to take GEC into the next century.</p>
<p>On Monday, The Times reported that GEC was poised to buy defence group Alenia Difensa. Alenia is controlled by state-owned Finmeccanica.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 7717</p>
